# Normalize line endings for all text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Large binary .wasm modules in this folder: no diffs, no merges, no line-ending
# munging. The `binary` macro sets -diff -merge -text, and -text overrides the
# `* text=auto` rule above.
#
# Deliberately NOT routed through Git LFS. Every module published so far is
# stored as a normal blob, and nothing in this repository consumes LFS: none of
# the workflows pass `lfs: true` to actions/checkout, so a checkout yields the
# 133-byte pointer instead of the module and the playground serves that text to
# WebAssembly.instantiate(), which fails with
#
#   expected magic word 00 61 73 6d, found 76 65 72 73
#
# ("vers", the start of "version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1"). The
# previous comment here claimed that without LFS the files "will be treated as
# binary", which is true of diffing but not of storage: a consumer without the
# LFS smudge filter gets pointer text on disk, not the module.
playground/assets/wasm/*.wasm binary

# The .mjs glue next to those modules is text and stays reviewable, but
# Emscripten pads some of its lines, so a rebuild makes `git diff --check`
# report trailing whitespace in generated output. Silence just that complaint:
# `whitespace=-blank-at-eol` drops the blank-at-eol check for these paths and
# nothing else.
playground/assets/wasm/*.mjs whitespace=-blank-at-eol
